    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Terrestrial carbon cycle and climate feedbacks",
    "problem": "Existing carbon-cycle-climate models struggle to accurately predict terrestrial ecosystem feedbacks due to a poor understanding of complex, interacting processes, such as soil carbon dynamics, and nonlinear responses to multi-factor environmental changes and climate extremes.",
    "method": "To improve the assessment of carbon-cycle feedbacks, the paper proposes a framework combining long-term multifactorial experiments, non-destructive ecosystem-level observations, and the integration of these results with ecosystem modelling in a multiple-constraint framework.",
    "task": "The task is to assess the complex feedback mechanisms between terrestrial ecosystem carbon dynamics and climate change, synthesizing current knowledge to evaluate how ecosystems will likely provide a positive, amplifying feedback in a warming world.",
